The generated semantics compiled cleanly and the fresh concrete runs agree with Python on the smallest composite, both branch directions, the square boundary, a semiprime, a power of two, and the documented large example. The loop-refinement claim independently closed with `#Top`; the universal entry claim is substantially slower and is still running under the fresh definition, so I’m continuing to monitor it rather than treating elapsed time as a result.
